<% content_for(:title, "InstantRecord Demos") %>

<div class="page home">
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="micro-label">InstantRecord</p>
    <h1>Rails models that run in the&nbsp;browser.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      These demos are ordinary Rails controllers and views — compiled to WebAssembly
      and rendered inside a service worker, backed by Postgres-in-the-browser.
      Writes commit locally and instantly, queue in a durable outbox, and sync to the
      server when you're online. Everyone else's changes stream back down over
      server-sent events. Go offline; keep working.
    </p>
    <p class="meta">
      Runtime: <strong><%= InstantRecord.browser? ? "browser (ruby.wasm + PGlite)" : "server (CRuby + Postgres)" %></strong>
    </p>
  </header>

  <ul class="demo-index">
    <li>
      <%= link_to todo_root_path, class: "demo-card" do %>
        <p class="micro-label">Demo 01</p>
        <h2>Todo</h2>
        <p>Optimistic local writes, and a server-only validation that rejects a
        title after the browser already accepted it.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      <% end %>
    </li>
    <li>
      <%= link_to slack_root_path, class: "demo-card" do %>
        <p class="micro-label">Demo 02</p>
        <h2>Swiss Slack</h2>
        <p>Channels, DMs, and fake users who reply from the server — watch their
        messages arrive over SSE without touching a WebSocket. Swag as we wack.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      <% end %>
    </li>
    <li>
      <%= link_to migrate_root_path, class: "demo-card" do %>
        <p class="micro-label">Demo 03</p>
        <h2>Ship v2</h2>
        <p>Fill a local database, leave writes unsynced, then run a migration over
        the top of it. Your rows and your queue both have to survive.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      <% end %>
    </li>
    <li>
      <%= link_to console_root_path, class: "demo-card" do %>
        <p class="micro-label">Demo 04</p>
        <h2>Console</h2>
        <p>No UI, no seeds, nothing staged — an ActiveRecord prompt against the
        database in this tab. Type a query the demo didn't anticipate.</p>
        <span class="go">Open →</span>
      <% end %>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="meta">
    <%= link_to "What this cost on your device →", receipts_path %>
  </p>

  <footer class="project-strip">
    <p class="micro-label">Open source</p>
    <p>
      InstantRecord is an MIT-licensed Ruby gem. These demos are its test bed —
      every page here is in the repo, and the source drawer below reads it out
      of the running bundle.
    </p>
    <p class="project-links">
      <a href="https://github.com/kieranklaassen/instant_record">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27s1.36.09 2 .27c1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/></svg>
        GitHub
      </a>
      <a href="https://rubygems.org/gems/instant_record">RubyGems</a>
      <code>gem "instant_record"</code>
    </p>
  </footer>
</div>
